    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a8b4cfac078047548276a87d5f4f29e5",
      "statement": "The PageIndex-vs-Weaviate gate (stage 1 only, since PageIndex lost stage 1) showed PageIndex trailing Weaviate on page_recall (0.609 vs 0.681 overall) and chunk_recall (0.601 vs 0.618), at roughly double the retrieval latency (3.10s vs 1.66s) and context size (8.2 vs 4.4 chunks/question), with total misses on three golden items where the node selector picked sections lacking the expected pages.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/decisions/pageindex-vs-weaviate.md#L16-L30",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:65d7bc4d3be1f1ba33c710d6f85fc599eabc111da4582d90fb452a78ac8dece0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ab51cb0275774ecdb80f3e018f0b69e6",
      "statement": "The Pinecone-rerank evaluation's stage 1 rejected the plain Pinecone hybrid arm (page_recall 0.463 vs a 0.648 Weaviate reference) and the Pinecone+rerank arm (0.504), while Weaviate+rerank passed stage 1 (0.698, +0.050); stage 2's paired judged eval then rejected Weaviate+rerank because correctness (0.799 vs 0.850, Δ−0.051), and holdout correctness (0.737 vs 0.828, Δ−0.091) both failed their thresholds even though cost and p50 latency passed, because the reranker returned chunks from the right pages but less complete content.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/decisions/pinecone-rerank.md#L19-L46",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b883e98d33c6ab1d8011cbeb6ef196030108adf6fef296e0ff9f031ef0c8640c:"
        }
