      "statement": "A labelled diagnostic (not used for arm selection) found that roughly 0.13 of the Pinecone hybrid arm's page_recall loss versus Weaviate came from an unnormalized convex combination of raw dot-product and raw sparse scores, with the remainder attributable to the dense-only index trailing a lexical+dense hybrid on the holdout split.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/decisions/pinecone-rerank.md#L27-L29",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8a469fba491b2317c7a6d972f1e60c657eca7d5c6e0c4dccd89424cc6f5277f9:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c84bc5a5a8574d1ebf01454281b4a915",
      "statement": "docs/retrieval-experiments.md documents that all three retrieval alternatives (PageIndex, Pinecone, reranking) were evaluated behind opt-in knobs using the same frozen two-stage paired gate and all three lost, so Weaviate hybrid search stays as the retrieval stage unchanged; the arms and gate are inert at runtime under default settings (HC_RAG_RETRIEVER=weaviate, HC_RAG_RERANKER=none) and are retained for any future retrieval proposal to be judged the same way.",
